<Base title="About" current="/about" description="What this archive is, what it is not, and how to reach us.">
  <div class="page ed">
    <h1>About this archive</h1>
    <p>The Nemeton Archive is a non-commercial fan project: a reading of Sacnoth’s <em>Koudelka</em> (1999) as a dossier, by Renan Botasse. It exists to collect, source and present what is known about the game's world, people, sound and legacy, and to show how a site can be part of the work it describes.</p>

    <h2>What this is not</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>It is not official, and it is not endorsed by any rights holder of <em>Koudelka</em>.</li>
      <li>It does not host the game, its music, its videos or its models, and it will not.</li>
      <li>It makes no money and has no ads.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Rights and credits</h2>
    <p><em>Koudelka</em> © its respective rights holders. The monastery you see on this site, the writing, the drawings and the sound are original. Where official material is shown, it is a small, credited piece of evidence under commentary. Who owns the game today is not publicly clear.</p>
    <p><strong>Takedown:</strong> if you hold rights in anything shown here and want it removed, write to the contact address published with the site's launch, and it will be removed promptly.</p>

    <h2>A note on language</h2>
    <p>The game and many fan wikis use an old, often offensive word for its protagonist's people. This archive uses <em>Romani</em> and <em>Roma</em>, and keeps the older word only inside unaltered quotations, with a note. Nothing here invents Romani culture.</p>

    <h2>Privacy and access</h2>
    <p>No cookies, no trackers and no third-party scripts. Fonts are served from this site. The site works without JavaScript and without WebGL, supports keyboard use, respects reduced-motion settings and aims at WCAG 2.2 AA.</p>
    <p class="mono"><a href="/made">How this was made</a> · Colophon: Astro, SolidJS, three.js. Fonts: Cinzel, Newsreader, IBM Plex Mono (all SIL OFL).</p>
  </div>
</Base>
